course: dictionary
lesson: 1320
title: Calculation: a sum or a plan
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A calculation is working out an answer using numbers, such as adding, subtracting, multiplying or dividing. In maths, you show your calculations so your teacher can see how you got your answer.
explain: The word has a second meaning too: careful planning or thinking about what will happen. «The first electronic computers, in the 1940s, filled whole rooms and were used to break codes and do huge calculations.» Here the computers were doing huge sums, so calculations means number work.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «An Islamic month begins when the thin new crescent moon is seen, or by calculation.» The words or by tell you that calculation is another way of working something out, instead of looking at the sky. Put your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Calculation means working out an answer using numbers.
fact: You can check a calculation with the inverse operation, or by estimating whether the answer is sensible.
fact: Mental calculation is done in your head; written calculation uses methods like column addition.
fact: Cold calculation means careful planning, often selfish, as in a calculating character who plans coldly in a story.
fact: «The old story that science proves bumblebees cannot fly came from a wrong simple calculation.» The sentence shows that a calculation can be wrong, so always check your working.
exercise: «The first electronic computers, in the 1940s, filled whole rooms and were used to break codes and do huge calculations.» What were the computers doing with calculations? | Singing to the people nearby | Painting pictures on the walls | *Working out huge sums with numbers | Planning their holidays
exercise: Ayesha checks 48 + 27 = 75 by doing 75 - 27 = 48. What is she checking with? | *The inverse operation | A guess about the weather | Column addition of the crescent moon | Cold calculation
exercise: Which phrase uses calculation to mean careful planning about what will happen? | *A cold calculation of who will win | Adding 6 and 7 on paper | Checking a sum with estimation | A written calculation in columns
test: «An Islamic month begins when the thin new crescent moon is seen, or by calculation.» Why might a month begin by calculation? | Because calculation means looking at the sky | Because the moon is too bright to see | Because every place sees the moon on the same day | *People work out in advance when the new moon will appear
test: Which example is a mental calculation? | Drawing a picture of a bumblebee | *Working out 9 + 5 in your head | Writing a long sum in columns on paper | Looking at the crescent moon through a telescope
exam: «The old story that science proves bumblebees cannot fly came from a wrong simple calculation.» What did the wrong calculation lead to? | A sum that the computers in the 1940s solved | Proof that bees cannot fly | Bees beating their wings more slowly | *A false idea that spread as if it were true
